# A working checkout of sst/opencode, needed to run the TUI and to resolve the maps'
# file:line citations. DERIVED, not authoritative — everything this project contributes to
# it lives in fork/ (17 files + the exact patch against base 7534d23). See fork/README.md
# to reconstitute this directory from scratch.
# NO TRAILING SLASH, and it is ONE rule rather than two. `/opencode/` matched a DIRECTORY
# only, so when a worktree bring-up made `opencode` a SYMLINK to another tree's checkout,
# `git add -A` TRACKED it — and the next commit, which replaced the symlink with a real
# checkout, turned it into a gitlink naming a submodule this repo does not declare. A clone
# would get an empty directory and `git submodule update --init` would fail with no mapping.
# MEASURED 2026-08-06 by doing exactly that. Keeping the old form beside this one would leave
# it the LAST matching pattern, so `git check-ignore -v opencode` would credit the dir-only
# rule this comment exists to explain away. TESTED in a scratch repo: the slashless form alone
# ignores the directory AND its contents AND the symlink.
/opencode

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Capture debris from the EXTERNAL gated-harness Claude Code plugin
# (~/.claude/plugins/cache/dev-harness/gated-harness/), not from anything in this repo. Its
# PostToolUse hook writes a {command, hash} record here on EVERY Bash call made by ANY Claude
# Code session whose cwd is this tree — including sessions doing unrelated reading. TESTED:
# three records accumulated during one investigation session, two of them capturing greps of
# the plugin's own source.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted because the plugin recreates the directory unprompted; the
# defect this guards is that `git add -A` was staging all three into a repo whose entire
# premise is that its artifacts are deliberate. Nothing in this project reads these files.
# There is no reaper for them, so prune by hand if the directory grows.
.harness/

# Per-change gate run records (gate/GATE.MAP.md). The plain <ts>.json records are DERIVED:
# re-runnable snapshots of a ~1.1s gate invocation, cheaper to regenerate than to keep. The
# <ts>-review.json records are NOT re-runnable (a model review is one nondeterministic
# judgment) and are kept ephemeral by choice, not because they can be regenerated; attach
# either kind to a PR deliberately when it is the evidence for that change. Do not
# accumulate every local run in the history.
gate/runs/

# Rig working state, SPLIT (2026-07-31 audit). hb/ holds two things with opposite
# lifecycles, and the previous comment here ("All DERIVED") was false for one of them.
#
# DERIVED scratch stays ignored: hb/project/ and the ledgers come back from rig.fixtures(),
# the free probes' own DBs (armdefault/armoff/armon, probe_on_grid, probe_load,
# controlwiring, reqchan, coldman) are recreated for free (all verified 0 sessions, or
# 60 no-model-turn sessions for reqchan), and *.db-wal / *.db-shm / *.log are transient
# SQLite sidecars and server logs. Set HEALBOT_RIG_WORK to move the scratch off the repo,
# but note the corpus below moves with it.
#
# The MEASUREMENT CORPUS is un-ignored below: the paid rigs' DBs are the hb/*.db corpus
# probe_turn_growth.py derives worst_turn from, they cost real API credits to create, and
# the rig README forbids deleting them ("that deletes the measurement"). WALs were
# checkpointed (TRUNCATE) before first tracking so the committed bytes are self-contained;
# re-checkpoint before committing a corpus update. Also tracked: ab-runs/ (paid A/B study
# rows, meta, server logs) and corpus-backups/ (the frozen-corpus safety net).
# A NEW PAID DB NEEDS ITS OWN NEGATION LINE HERE, or it is silently unprotected.
#
# The inverse also has a case, measured 2026-08-06: errorstate.db and focus.db were negated
# here until that date and did NOT belong. Neither is paid (probe_error_state.py's docstring:
# "Zero model turns, zero API credits") and neither is authored: both are
# `shutil.copyfile(db("retire350"), ...)`, probe_error_state.py:43 and probe_focus.py:59, so
# every probe run overwrote the tracked file with a fresh copy of retire350.db and dirtied the
# tree. The whole recurring diff was one cell, `project.time_updated`; no session, message or
# measurement row ever differed. retire350.db stays tracked and rebuilds both on demand, and
# probe_turn_growth.py dedupes its corpus (probe_turn_growth.py:305), so their absence changes
# no derivation. Do not re-add negation lines for them.
.carryover/verified/hb/*
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-runs/
!.carryover/verified/hb/corpus-backups/
!.carryover/verified/hb/quest.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/quest-phase12a.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/coldq.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/control.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/retire350.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/headless.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/autoretire.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/cold.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/focusexplore.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/smoke.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-full-stock.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-full-harness.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-pilot-stock.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-pilot-harness.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-pilot-v2-stock.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/ab-refusal-pilot-v2-harness.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/study-refusal-tdd-pilot-1-base.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/study-refusal-tdd-pilot-1-plus-tdd.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/study-refusal-tdd-full-1-base.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/study-refusal-tdd-full-1-plus-tdd.db
!.carryover/verified/hb/submit-verify-20260805/
